# Licensing overview

Short version: **do anything you like with this, including selling it, and you
do not have to credit anyone.**

| What | Licence | SPDX | File |
|---|---|---|---|
| Code, scripts, adapters, tools, tests | BSD Zero Clause | `0BSD` | [`LICENSE-CODE`](LICENSE-CODE) |
| Meshes, textures, materials, animations, schemas, catalogs, documentation | Creative Commons Zero v1.0 Universal | `CC0-1.0` | [`LICENSE-ASSETS`](LICENSE-ASSETS) |

Both licences permit, with no conditions attached:

- use, for any purpose
- copying and redistribution
- modification
- commercial use
- inclusion in paid products
- building on it and charging for your own work immediately

Neither requires attribution, notice retention, source disclosure, or a
share-alike licence on your derivatives. 0BSD is a public-domain-equivalent
permissive licence with no attribution clause; CC0 is a public-domain
dedication. The split exists only because CC0 is the right instrument for
creative assets and 0BSD is the right instrument for code — not because the
permissions differ.

## Why you can trust that

Every file in this repository is generated from scratch by scripts in this
repository. No third-party mesh, texture, model, scan or asset library is read
at any point in the pipeline, so there is nothing here whose rights could be
unclear.

That claim is auditable rather than asserted:

- every asset carries a per-asset `provenance` record naming the exact function
  that generated it, when, from what inputs (none), and under what origin
- `provenance/manifest.json` records a SHA-256 for every generated file
- `tessera validate` **fails** an asset whose provenance or licence fields are
  incomplete, and fails any asset marked `third-party` without a completed
  licence review
- see [`docs/provenance-policy.md`](docs/provenance-policy.md) for the quarantine
  rule for anything uncertain

## Contributing

By submitting a contribution you confirm you have the right to release it under
these terms. See [`CONTRIBUTING.md`](CONTRIBUTING.md).
